## Benchmark transfer

- Buffer: unfinished writing and draft/approval/queue states informed state preservation and approval separation.
- Sprout: approve/change-request activity informed same-item revision and approval expiry.
- Hootsuite: accountable external approval informed explicit reviewer consequence.
- Later: per-profile customization and unsupported reasons informed variant tabs and row-level bulk exclusions.
- Canva: create/calendar/analytics continuity informed result index and schedule linkage.
- HubSpot: source remix informed fixed Text → Photo/Card → Video, while v18 adds approved source lineage.
- Notion: import scope and Markdown behavior informed eligible/selected/skipped and product-wiki lifecycle.

What was not copied: competitor visual systems, plan limits, access-group language, generic template galleries or automatic posting defaults.

## Psychology contract audit

| problem | principle | UI decision | misuse guard |
|---|---|---|---|
| first use exposes 26 choices | progressive disclosure | one next action plus optional full sidebar | no forced tour; expert jumps and exits |
| generated claims may be trusted too much | calibrated trust | source/version and missing-evidence view | no confidence percentage |
| defaults change consequential behavior | defaults effect | publish and Messaging OFF | no hidden opt-out or prechecked consent |
| long setup feels unearned | endowed progress | only saved/confirmed steps complete | viewing/jumping never completes |
| many variants overload unfamiliar users | heterogeneous choice-overload evidence | family grouping and reversible recommendation | never claim fewer is always better |
| publish retry can duplicate | user control/error prevention | approval, preflight, uncertain and repair-only | uncertain retry disabled |

## Red team retake

Competitor attack: “It still has more steps than Buffer and less proven execution.”

Revision: quick one-off publishing stays available, while agency mode adds source version, brief, revision, result and experiment lineage. External execution remains explicitly unverified rather than hidden by a success demo.

Demanding customer attack: “My brief disappeared before; why trust the retake?”

Revision: four journey fields, eight variants and wiki content are now round-trip asserted. Same work/revision appears in Studio, Inbox, Calendar and results. Real browser and server persistence are still not claimed.

Skeptical investor attack: “A static DOM test can be gamed.”

Answer: correct. The audit now fails missing names, unregistered handlers and owner recovery no-ops, but JSDOM cannot validate visible pixels. The newest retake still needs the parent’s 12-combination screenshots and computed-style checks.

## Self-question

이 단계가 틀렸다면 가장 그럴듯한 이유는?

The load-bearing risk is that immutable local objects and 181 passing selectors look like product persistence, or that the 116KB prototype remains visually dense or keyboard-hostile. The correction is the explicit evidence split: DOM-observed is not server/provider evidence, and JSDOM zero-size rectangles cannot close the actual-browser gate.

If this is a simple publishing tool rather than a marketing agency, what is missing?

It would lack an approved client brief, resolvable brand-source version, creative rationale across three families, accountable approval, reusable result index and evidence-linked next experiment. All six are present at interaction-design level. Their server ownership and customer retention value remain unverified.

