## FINAL M14 retake-3 — customer language closure candidate

Independent v4 status at intake: **B+ / FINAL NO-GO, 13 of 14 majors resolved; only M14 open.** Exact defect was customer-default Studio and downstream dialogs/recovery/results/experiment exposing `cmp_`, `cnt_`, `rev_`, `pub_`, `ext_`, `exp_` values.

### What changed

- Customer UI now renders campaign title, work-family name, `수정 7/8`, request/confirm time, channel/account, publish status, metric and experiment name.
- The shared lineage strip translates all six immutable fields into customer vocabulary and uses `캠페인 진행 정보` as its accessible name.
- Studio, video, Calendar, variant/bulk/schedule/preview/preflight/result dialogs, 14-step journey, recovery cards/outcomes and next-experiment summaries were swept.
- Result accessible names no longer contain external IDs. Next-experiment sources render platform/status/metric summaries.
- Exact immutable IDs remain unchanged in frozen objects, `data-*`, recovery preservation records and `window.__V18_TEST_API__`; result reorder and revision apply/undo still key on them.
- `window.__V18_CUSTOMER_LANGUAGE_AUDIT__` scans customer root text, form values, `aria-label`, title and alt for raw prefixes and defined implementation-jargon blacklist entries.

